      "content": "4.1 Jurisdiction of Civil Courts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Defines the procedural laws governing civil litigation in India under the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908.",
        "Outlines the rules and parameters for the Jurisdiction of Civil Courts.",
        "Details key CPC provisions for filing suits, summons, decrees, and executions.",
        "Integrates the Limitation Act, 1963, which sets legal time limits for instituting civil suits and appeals."
      ],
      "id": "9hqmbtl"
