      "content": "Jurisdiction of Civil Courts",
      "id": "5zqq5ok"
    },
    {
      "id": "yi0ls67",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type of Jurisdiction</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Subject Matter Jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Court must have power to hear a particular type of case (e.g., family court for matrimonial disputes, consumer forum for consumer cases)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Territorial Jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Court must be within the territory where cause of action arises, or defendant resides or works, or property is situated</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pecuniary Jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Court must be empowered to adjudicate claims up to that value; e.g., civil judge has limit; district court is unlimited</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Original Jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Court that hears case at first instance; original; not on appeal</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Appellate Jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Court that hears appeals from lower courts</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nu2u63g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Important CPC Provisions"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4scggh",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Section/Order</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Subject</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 9</p>",
            "<p>Civil court jurisdiction</p>",
            "<p>Courts to try all civil suits unless expressly or impliedly barred</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 10</p>",
            "<p>Stay of suit (Res Sub Judice)</p>",
            "<p>If same matter pending in another court of competent jurisdiction between same parties, later suit to be stayed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 11</p>",
            "<p>Res Judicata</p>",
            "<p>Matter decided by court of competent jurisdiction cannot be reopened in subsequent suit between same parties on same subject matter</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 12</p>",
            "<p>Bar to further suit</p>",
            "<p>Where plaintiff omits to sue on any portion of claim, cannot later sue for that portion</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 16–20</p>",
            "<p>Place of suing</p>",
            "<p>Suits relating to immovable property — at place of property; personal suits — at defendant's place</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 47</p>",
            "<p>Questions to be determined by Court</p>",
            "<p>Court that passed decree decides all questions related to execution</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 80</p>",
            "<p>Notice to Government</p>",
            "<p>2-month prior notice required before filing suit against Government or public officer</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Section 89</p>",
            "<p>Alternate Dispute Resolution</p>",
            "<p>Court can refer matter to Arbitration, Conciliation, Judicial Settlement, Mediation, Lok Adalat</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 1</p>",
            "<p>Parties to suits</p>",
            "<p>Who can be joined as plaintiff or defendant; representative suits</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 6</p>",
            "<p>Pleadings</p>",
            "<p>Plaint and Written Statement; principles: concise statement of material facts, not evidence; no legal arguments</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 7</p>",
            "<p>Plaint</p>",
            "<p>Must contain: court, parties, cause of action, facts, relief claimed, limitation plea</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 8</p>",
            "<p>Written Statement</p>",
            "<p>Defendant's response; must deny specifically or be deemed admitted; limitation defence must be pleaded</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 9</p>",
            "<p>Appearance and non-appearance</p>",
            "<p>Ex-parte decree if defendant absent; setting aside ex-parte decree</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 37</p>",
            "<p>Summary Suit</p>",
            "<p>For recovery of money on bills of exchange, cheques, promissory notes; defendant must get leave to defend</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 38–40</p>",
            "<p>Attachment before judgment, arrest before judgment, appointment of receiver</p>",
            "<p>Interim reliefs</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 39</p>",
            "<p>Temporary Injunctions</p>",
            "<p>Three conditions: Prima facie case; Balance of convenience; Irreparable harm/injury</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Order 43</p>",
            "<p>Appeals from orders</p>",
            "<p>Appeals against specific orders</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Section 9 of CPC regarding the civil courts' authority to try suits of a civil nature unless barred is frequently asked.",
        "Understanding the distinction between pecuniary, territorial, and subject-matter jurisdiction is essential for competitive law exams.",
        "Key prescribed periods under the Limitation Act, 1963 are high-yield topics in Judicial Service Exams."
      ],
      "id": "w145um1"
    },
